mpleted":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nReproducible in: Godot 4.7 dev 3 (Godot Engine v4.7.dev3.official)\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.7.dev3 - Windows 11 (build 26200) - Multi-window, 1 monitor - Direct3D 12 (Forward+) - dedicated NVIDIA GeForce GTX 1050 (NVIDIA; 32.0.15.8180) - Intel(R) Core(TM) i5-8300H CPU @ 2.30GHz (8 threads) - 11.85 GiB memory\n\n### Issue description\n\nWhen using the newly added MeshInstance3D gizmos (just like in CSG nodes), i get a weird twitch or flick coming from the inspector after using and releasing the mesh gizmos.\nI tested in a newly created project using the Forward+ renderer, adding a MeshInstance3D node and assigning a mesh to it (BoxMesh in my case). When the gizmos appeared, i used them and after i release/use the gizmo i see the inspector twitching out weirdly for a very short period of time.\nThis does not happen when using the CSG mesh nodes gizmos.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nas explained above, open a new project in Godot 4.7 dev 3, in the editor, add a MeshInstance3D node and assign a mesh to it (primitives are recommended for testing). Then, use the gizmos that appear in the mesh and after releasing the action (using the gizmo) watch the inspector dock (if available) and you will notice a strange \"flick\" coming from it.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nN/A","closed_by":{"login":"matheusmdx","id":44306054,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0MzA2MDU0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/44306054?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/matheusmdx","html_url":"https://github.com/matheusmdx","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matheusmdx/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matheusmdx/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matheusmdx/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mathe